      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code. i checked the manual but im not really sure what to do. how do i check the leak sensor and dry out the base?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, to check the leak sensor, locate it near the door; it may be outlined in the manual. Remove any elements (fruits, vegetables, filters) inside the dishwasher. Unplug the appliance, remove any plastic drawers, and rinse off all the parts. Use a towel to dry the exterior and a hair dryer or a hot air gun to dry the base and internal parts to ensure there are no water leaks. After drying, power the appliance back on, put the racks in place, add a cleaning or heavy-duty cleaner tablet, close the door, and run a short cleaning cycle. If the leak sensor doesn't clean off, the sensor may be faulty and needs replacement. You may need professional help if you're not comfortable fixing it yourself.",
